WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.268
 Rita, Justin, congratulations.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.936
You guys have made
it to the final round

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.338
of this competition.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.339
Now it's time to send you
back to your home forges

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:10.877
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.278
And that weapon is--

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.683
the sodegarami.

00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:18.517
 Holy.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.386
Jeez.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:21.687
Oh my god.

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:22.688
MAN: Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:23.656
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:30.296
 I've never made a
sodegarami in my life.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.565
First time I've ever heard of
it was when they unveiled it.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:35.668
It's going to be a learning
experience for everybody.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.103
I'm going to make Damascus.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:41.073
My goal today is just to
get a few billets welded up.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.642
So we're going to
do a 15 and 20.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:46.379
We'll clean that first, and
then we'll move on to our 1084

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.346
and clean that up.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.681
I'm not going to
go crazy with it.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:52.218
I don't want to do
anything super elaborate.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.819
The next process
is going to be just

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:56.656
welding these bad boys together
and getting a billet together.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.462
Day one in the books.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:03.530
Things went pretty well.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.997
We got a couple of
billets welded up.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:08.134
Tomorrow we'll be
making spikes and doing

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.669 line:14%
all kinds of fun stuff.

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:14.707 line:8%
 Day three, yesterday, I was
able to finish up my spikes.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:17.243
I got all of my tines started.

00:01:17.309 --> 00:01:21.714
Today I am going to
start with my entangler.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:22.949
Super awesome.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.684
For this sodegarami,
I'm going to have

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.585
the theme of the octopus.

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:29.388
The octopus is an animal
that entangles its prey,

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:32.291
and I think that's a fitting
theme for this weapon.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:37.830
So I want my entangler to
emote octopus tentacles.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.398
Ah.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.167
It's time for me to quench.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.239
Woo-hoo.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.641
My quench went well.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:52.578
The head of the sodegarami
looks pretty good.

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:55.081
At the end of day three,
everything is built,

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.617
and I can start putting
this together tomorrow.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:02.922 line:8%
 Day three, we're going to
try to do some heat treat,

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.758
make sure this thing's ready
to put together and test.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.660
I cut the billet
into four pieces.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:10.430
I'm going to forge these
out into the four spikes

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:13.399
in the front of the sodegarami.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.000
Hoping I'm going
to start shaping

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.736
these and pulling
little leaves off them

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.638
to do some backwards barbs.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.473
Coming together.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.476
For the handle, I'm using
a curly ambrosia maple.

00:02:25.878 --> 00:02:26.846
Feels pretty solid.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.015
Feel like a Ninja Turtle.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:29.883
It's time to quench.

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:33.753
Go ahead and harden
just the blade.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.256
Leave the rest soft so
that when they smack it

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.090
into whatever they're going
to smack it in, hopefully

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:39.392
it won't break.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:41.693
Just quenched five blades.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:42.962
My back hurts.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.096
My legs hurt, but
you got one more day.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:46.866 line:14%
Got to knock it out.

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.568 line:8%
 Halfway through
the last day, I

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.370
plan to have this
sodegarami built.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.371
I'm feeling pretty good
after getting to spend

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.908
this time on the weapon.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.642
I'm excited to see
that I could do it,

00:02:56.709 --> 00:03:00.980
and I'm excited for my daughter
and my scouts to see, too.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.316
[non-english speech]

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.253
Done pretty much
everything I wanted to do,

00:03:07.319 --> 00:03:09.822
but I have time to
do one more thing.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:10.990
Stab.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.891
So I test my sodegarami
one more time.

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:13.893
Yoink.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.663
And I hear a little noise.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.565
Ah!

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:20.934
Oh, [bleep].

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.201
I got to fix this.

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:23.435
Son of a [bleep].

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:25.838
I spent a lot of
time on this weapon,

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.440
and I've broken this thing.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:30.943
So I'm just going to run back
and put whatever kind of crappy

00:03:31.043 --> 00:03:32.110
weld I can get on it.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:33.680
If this doesn't
work, I'm screwed.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:38.417 line:8%
 Day four, ready to get
this thing assembled.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.285
Got about 1,000
different processes

00:03:40.352 --> 00:03:41.420
to get through today--

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:43.322
sharpening spikes,
welding spikes,

00:03:43.388 --> 00:03:46.092
blade sharpening and shaping.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:49.195
Got about 1,000 tasks.

00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:51.664
A little Mongolian horse hair.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.233
That is a blood guard.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.438
[bleep]

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.906
Putting the head in, and it
seems like it wanted to split

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:04.710
on me, so we're going to throw a
little bit of epoxy and leather

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.246
around this thing and
call it what it is.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.814
If something goes
wrong with my weapon,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.050
it's going to be that I
wasn't able to pin the head.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:12.417
Just didn't have
the time to do it.

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:14.120
Hopefully it stays together.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.455
Sodegarami build is done.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:20.393
She might not be pretty,
but she will KEAL.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.427
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:24.130
Welcome to the KEAL test.

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:27.499
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your sodegarami will do,

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:29.202
I will take your
weapons and stab

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.704
and try to snag this
ballistics dummy.

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.338
Rita, you're up first.

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.406
You ready for this?

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.040
 Aye.

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:49.022
[laughs]

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:01.934
[laughs]

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:05.938
 All right, Rita.

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:07.640
Let's talk about
your sodegarami.

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:10.243
The tines you have
here penetrates.

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:13.412
The hook you have here
will rip this person apart,

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:18.885
and, more importantly,
your weapon will KEAL.

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:19.985
All right, Justin.
Your turn.

00:05:20.052 --> 00:05:20.753
You ready to have fun?

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:21.587
 Yes, sir.

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.680
 All right, Justin.

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:51.016
The tines you have here,
it's more of a stabbing tine

00:05:51.116 --> 00:05:52.251
rather than a grabbing.

00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:53.986
And this is a
grabbing weapon, but

00:05:54.052 --> 00:05:56.155
that hook does grab on to that.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:59.892
Overall, sir, your
weapon will KEAL.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.461
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:05.898
It's time for the strength test,
the dreaded ice block chop.

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:08.033
Remember, this is not
about what these weapons

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:09.569
do to the ice blocks.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.871
It's about what those ice
blocks do to your weapons.

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.405
And, Rita, you're up first.

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:14.807
You get points for theme.

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:17.610
I mean-- [laughs]

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:19.478
You ready?

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:20.446
It doesn't matter, right?

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:23.015
 No, it doesn't matter.

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:25.718
[grunting]

00:06:47.072 --> 00:06:48.441
 All, right, Rita.

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:52.211
You a little bit more of a
bend in this one tine here.

00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:56.048
But everything else is pretty
much the way it was going in.

00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:57.316
Definitely held up.
Did its job.

00:06:57.383 --> 00:06:58.050
Good job.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:06:59.151
 Thank you.

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:00.219
 All right, Justin.

00:07:00.285 --> 00:07:01.253
Your turn.
You ready?

00:07:01.353 --> 00:07:02.422
 Yes, I am.

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:32.618
 All right, so you
survived the strength test.

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:35.921
This is a very strong,
well-built head for this,

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:40.092
but it's built more like a
spear than it is for catching.

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:41.794
I mean, I'm not
sure how effective

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:44.296
it would be at
snagging the opponent,

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:45.932
but it's a devastator.

00:07:46.032 --> 00:07:47.166
It certainly did the job.

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:48.267
Good job.

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:49.835
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:07:49.935 --> 00:07:54.707
Welcome to the sharpness test,
the sandman pierce and capture.

00:07:54.774 --> 00:07:56.909
To test the sharpness,
I will take your weapon,

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:59.612
pierce, and try to
control this sandman.

00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:00.479
Rita, you're first.

00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:01.280
You ready for this?

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.148
 Yeah.

00:08:25.604 --> 00:08:26.772
 All right, Rita.

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:28.473
The points you have
on your tines here

00:08:28.574 --> 00:08:31.443
definitely penetrate when
you thrust into that,

00:08:31.543 --> 00:08:33.712
but doesn't slice on
the way out or capture

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.481
as well as it should.

00:08:35.547 --> 00:08:37.749
Your hook over here did its job.

00:08:37.816 --> 00:08:40.920
Overall, it will
cut and control.

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:42.221
All right, Justin.
Your turn, sir.

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:42.955
Are you ready?

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:43.856
 Yes, I am.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.209
 That's not good.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:10.582
 (WHISPERING) He pulled
it out of the socket.

00:09:10.683 --> 00:09:12.785
 Well, Justin,
we have a problem.

00:09:12.852 --> 00:09:13.819
 Yes, sir.

00:09:13.919 --> 00:09:15.187
 This wasn't pinned, was it?

00:09:15.287 --> 00:09:16.622
 No.

00:09:16.689 --> 00:09:18.457
 The impact from all
these tests loosened it up,

00:09:18.557 --> 00:09:20.293
and, of course, it came off.

00:09:22.928 --> 00:09:26.565
 Justin, you brought in a
beautifully-crafted weapon.

00:09:26.632 --> 00:09:29.034
However, you've suffered
a catastrophic failure

00:09:29.134 --> 00:09:30.636
in our final test.

00:09:30.736 --> 00:09:32.538
And, unfortunately,
you cannot be

00:09:32.604 --> 00:09:34.239
our "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:34.306 --> 00:09:35.140
 Congratulations, Rita.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:36.041
 Thank you.

00:09:36.141 --> 00:09:37.443
It was beautiful.

00:09:37.509 --> 00:09:39.345
 Coming on "Forged in Fire,"
I proved what I wanted to do,

00:09:39.445 --> 00:09:41.213
that people with
physical limitations

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.782
can do as well as anybody.

00:09:42.848 --> 00:09:45.651
I put my all into it, and I
feel like I made a good weapon.

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:47.252
But just came up
short on a little bit

00:09:47.319 --> 00:09:50.089
of the fit and finish, and other
than that, I'm happy with it.

00:09:52.825 --> 00:09:54.527
 Rita, congratulations.

00:09:54.627 --> 00:09:56.795
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:56.862 --> 00:10:00.532
and that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:10:00.599 --> 00:10:02.068
Congratulations.

00:10:02.168 --> 00:10:04.503
How do you feel right now?

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:05.704
 I'm just--

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:08.106
 Come on forward
and shake our hands.

00:10:08.173 --> 00:10:09.174
Good job.

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:11.009
 It's been a very
positive and uplifting

00:10:11.076 --> 00:10:14.246
experience to be able to do
something amazing like this.

00:10:14.346 --> 00:10:17.983
I hope this will help me
become an inspiration to kids

00:10:18.049 --> 00:10:20.652
because I can say, look,
if you see something

00:10:20.719 --> 00:10:22.854
and you want to try
it, give it a try.

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:25.257
Hey, Weeblos, your scout
leader is the new "Forged

00:10:25.323 --> 00:10:26.191
in Fire" champion.

00:10:26.258 --> 00:10:27.459
I'm bringing it home.

00:10:27.525 --> 00:10:29.127
Can I have a group hug, please?

00:10:29.194 --> 00:10:30.029
[laughter]

00:10:30.096 --> 00:10:31.196
Thank you, you guys.

00:10:31.263 --> 00:10:33.165
Oh my god.

